<article class="env-lemma" id="096L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/096L">Lemma <span data-tag="096L">61.3.8</span>.</a> Let $A$ be a ring. Set $X = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$. The functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  B \longmapsto \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)  \]
</div>
  <p> from the category of $A$-algebras $B$ such that $A \to B$ identifies local rings to the category of topological spaces over $X$ is fully faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/096K" data-tag="096K">61.3.7</a> and the fact that if $A \to B$ identifies local rings, then the pullback of the structure sheaf of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ via $p : \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is equal to the structure sheaf of $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>